1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,067
Hello and welcome to today's 'Buyer Beware' programme,

2
00:00:03,067 --> 00:00:08,050
where we give you some tips on how to spend your money wisely.

3
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:12,830
Now, in today's show we're looking at beds for children and babies.

4
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:18,140
Let's start by looking at baby cots, that's for children of up to three years old.

5
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:22,758
We tested three different cots all in the budget price range and,

6
00:00:22,758 --> 00:00:27,760
as usual, we will feature the good points, the problems and our verdict.

7
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:32,160
The first cot we looked at was by Baby Safe

8
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:34,740
and it had several good points to recommend it.

9
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:40,700
Our testers liked the fact that it had four wheels, so it was easy to move around.

10
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:44,674
The only slight problems with this cot were that it had no brakes,

11
00:00:44,674 --> 00:00:47,120
but they didn't think that mattered too much.

12
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:50,560
At first they were a bit concerned about the side bar

13
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:53,676
because they felt babies could trap their fingers in it,

14
00:00:53,676 --> 00:00:56,440
but our testers felt that this was unlikely to happen

15
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:59,920
so they have given this one a verdict of 'satisfactory'.

16
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:06,541
The next cot was by Choice Cots and this time our testers were pleased to find a cot

17
00:01:06,541 --> 00:01:10,220
which is simple to put together-unlike others we looked at.

18
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:16,621
On the minus side, our testers did not like the fact that the side of the cot did not drop down,

19
00:01:16,621 --> 00:01:19,060
making it difficult to pick up newborn babies.

20
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:23,220
However, the real problem with this cot was the space between the bars;

21
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:28,020
our testers found they were too wide and a baby could easily trap his head.

22
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:31,120
We felt this was a real safety hazard and

23
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:34,000
so we have labelled this one dangerous, I'm afraid.

24
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,850
And finally better news for the Mother's Choice cot.

25
00:01:37,850 --> 00:01:43,068
This cot was slightly different in that, although the side bar did not drop down,

26
00:01:43,068 --> 00:01:49,330
the base could be raised or lowered into two different positions making it safe as well as convenient.

27
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:52,620
The negatives for this one were quite minor

28
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:56,031
the only niggle everyone had was the fact that it has no wheels

29
00:01:56,031 --> 00:01:58,584
and the only other problem anyone could find,

30
00:01:58,584 --> 00:02:01,780
was that there were pictures which were simply stuck on

31
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:03,690
and so could easily become detached.

32
00:02:03,690 --> 00:02:07,060
The makers have now promised to discontinue this practice.

33
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:10,582
As this cot will then be safe in every way,

34
00:02:10,582 --> 00:02:15,160
we have made the Mother's Choice cot our best buy. Congratulations Mother's Choice!

35
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:19,200
So, what features should you look for in a baby's cot?

36
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:25,140
Well obviously safety is a very important factor as well as comfort and convenience.

37
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:28,001
We recommend that, if you are buying a cot,

38
00:02:28,001 --> 00:02:32,770
do make sure that any metal present is not rusted or bent in any way.

39
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:39,159
You should ensure your cot has only rounded or smooth edging without any sharp edges,

40
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:42,140
this is especially important for wooden cots.

41
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:45,150
And now on to beds for toddlers...
